       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **50 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose for depression or anxiety.\n- **100 mg PO once daily**, a common therapeutic dose. This may be what you meant if the extra zero was a typo.\n- **200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose.\n\nTell me the dose and indication you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is what you want, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
